  "summary": "The third proposal's file-specific fix strategy is mostly sound, but it has a critical error regarding index.html: it says to 'remove var key = getKey()' in the edit functions (lines 763/804/842/900) and rely on the existing closure variable 'key' from line 386. This is correct in principle — the IIFE at line 386 defines 'key' in the Authenticated block's script scope and the edit functions at lines 762-900 are in the same script block, so they can access it. However, all three proposals miss a silent regression risk: in client.html, the edit functions (lines 1117/1158/1196/1254) use getKey() which re-reads from localStorage/URL on every call, meaning if the key rotates or is updated during the session, edits pick up the new key. Replacing with the static _dashKey (set once from Go template at page load) loses this dynamic behavior. This is likely acceptable since _dashKey comes from the server-rendered value which is already validated, but it's worth noting. The concrete fix is simple and all proposals agree on the core approach: (1) in client.html, replace the four 'var key = getKey()' lines in clientSaveEditTitle/Type/Description/DoneScript with 'var key = _dashKey' since _dashKey is always defined at line 497; (2) in index.html, remove the four 'var key = getKey()' lines in saveEditTitle/Type/Description/DoneScript since the closure variable 'key' from the IIFE at line 386 is already in scope; (3) in index.html, move restartClient() (line 1094) out of the ShowKeyModal block or refactor it to use the Authenticated block's 'key' variable, since it currently calls getKey() and would fail for authenticated users. The logout() duplication (defined at both lines 455 and 1090 in index.html, and line 331 in client.html) is not blocking since the Authenticated block's version at line 455 takes precedence for dashboard users, and client.html's logout at line 331 is only needed during the ShowKeyModal flow."
